# Page & App Architecture

## Before building a page or feature
1. Read relevant docs under `docs/context/` and any existing `docs/pages/<page>.md`.
2. Create or update `docs/pages/<page-name>.md` from `docs/pages/_TEMPLATE.md` (purpose, functions, **page-logic Mermaid flowchart**).
3. Follow [UI_THEME.md](../../docs/context/UI_THEME.md) — do not invent a conflicting look.

## App shell
- Persistent nav/chrome; only the **content area** loads or swaps.
- Shell tab changes: no slide animation (`IndexedStack`).
- Pages pushed **outside** the shell (detail, signup, onboarding edit): use `AppPageRoutes.slideFromRight` (slide from right).

## Separation
- Logic/functions separate from UI/design. Reusable themed widgets for buttons, cards, skeletons.

## Page UX
- Cache last-known data when possible.
- Skeleton loaders show structure immediately.
- Optimistic UI for actions that should normally succeed; on failure rollback + visible error.
- Prefer realtime listeners/streams (e.g. Supabase Realtime). “Subscription” means code listener, not paid billing.

## Cost
- Prefer **free** APIs and free tiers; document limits when choosing a service.
